------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS (parity scope)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GotoIndicator.tsx is a PURE presentational keyboard-shortcut hint. Its entire surface area:
  • Props      : { visible: boolean }
  • Data hooks : useTranslation ONLY (i18n) — NO query, NO fetch, NO formatting, NO shared components,
                 NO charts, NO maps.
  • Branches   : `if (!visible) return null;`  then a bottom-centred frosted pill:
                 <span muted>{t('shortcuts.goto','Go to...')}</span> <kbd>g</kbd> <span>+</span> <kbd>?</kbd>
  • i18n keys  : exactly one — `shortcuts.goto` (fallback "Go to..."). The `g` / `?` key glyphs and the
                 `+` chord separator are language-neutral keyboard symbols rendered verbatim (not translated).

=> The source has EXACTLY TWO states: hidden (`!visible` ⇒ renders nothing) and visible (the chord).
   There is NO async / data / freshness dimension, so the leaf-template loading/empty/error/stale/offline
   axes DO NOT EXIST in this source and were deliberately NOT fabricated (covenant rules 2 & 9 — adding
   them would be invented behaviour / silent drift). Both real branches are reproduced and tested.

